WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.320
Imagine you were out in public and you found
yourself injured.

00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:08.980
Maybe you were in an accident and couldn’t
move, or someone had mugged you in the ensuing

00:00:08.980 --> 00:00:11.490
scuffle you’d ended up getting hurt.

00:00:11.490 --> 00:00:15.411
Laying on the cold, filthy concrete of the
sidewalk, in desperate need of help, what

00:00:15.411 --> 00:00:19.930
could be the one thing that might make you
feel even the slightest bit better?

00:00:19.930 --> 00:00:24.470
Something the very sight of would be enough
to tell you everything was going to be okay.

00:00:24.470 --> 00:00:29.039
The flashing lights drawing closer, accompanied
by the sound of tires on the road and a wailing

00:00:29.039 --> 00:00:32.640
siren; all signs that an ambulance is on its
way.

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:37.230
But what if the ambulance that came to assist
you ended up making you feel far worse than

00:00:37.230 --> 00:00:42.739
you were before… and leaving you with injuries
unlike anything you’d ever seen?

00:00:42.739 --> 00:00:48.109
What if it wasn’t an ambulance at all that
came to help you, what if you were found by

00:00:48.109 --> 00:00:51.519
SCP-4419 instead?

00:00:51.519 --> 00:00:56.040
Jeremy had been having a somewhat normal day
until his accident.

00:00:56.040 --> 00:01:00.440
Work had been another shift of long, arduous
hours spent behind his desk.

00:01:00.440 --> 00:01:04.670
Five o’clock finally rolled around, he grabbed
his bag and punched out.

00:01:04.670 --> 00:01:10.070
If he’d maybe left a few minutes later,
he might have gotten away unscathed.

00:01:10.070 --> 00:01:13.630
Instead of getting caught in the mad rush
of people leaving work, Jeremy usually took

00:01:13.630 --> 00:01:17.640
the backstreets and avoided main roads as
a shortcut to get home.

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:22.200
There was less traffic, even during the rush,
and that made crossing the street safer…

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:23.200
usually.

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:28.119
He had been looking the other way when a car
came speeding down the mostly-empty side street.

00:01:28.119 --> 00:01:32.840
The driver had slammed the breaks, but only
too late, knocking Jeremy down.

00:01:32.840 --> 00:01:38.509
Winded, he collapsed, unable to stand as the
force of the impact had broken his leg.

00:01:38.509 --> 00:01:43.609
The driver and a few nearby onlookers huddled
around Jeremy as he lay there with his injury.

00:01:43.609 --> 00:01:48.409
Suddenly, the noise of an ambulance caused
the other pedestrians to mostly disperse.

00:01:48.409 --> 00:01:53.200
Still trying to catch his breath, in the last
moments of his fading consciousness, the last

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:56.399
thing Jeremy remembered seeing was a pair
of figures.

00:01:56.399 --> 00:02:01.479
They had jostled rather aggressively through
the crowd, reaching down to lift Jeremy up

00:02:01.479 --> 00:02:04.569
and shoved him into the emergency vehicle.

00:02:04.569 --> 00:02:10.191
They were considerably rude for medical professionals,
nobody around wanted to argue with them; most

00:02:10.191 --> 00:02:12.660
would even go as far as to call them hostile.

00:02:12.660 --> 00:02:17.690
But that was nothing compared to the horror
that awaited him when he reopened his eyes,

00:02:17.690 --> 00:02:20.400
laying back on the road where he’d been
found.

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:24.890
His body had been rearranged, he barely recognized
it as his own.

00:02:24.890 --> 00:02:30.540
It was like he had been turned into some grotesque
animal made using human parts.

00:02:30.540 --> 00:02:36.860
His arms and legs had been rearranged to protrude
from his torso in an unnatural configuration.

00:02:36.860 --> 00:02:43.200
What felt even worse was that his fingers,
toes, hands, feet… they all still worked.

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:50.100
All Jeremy could do was scream until he slipped
back under, a man turned into something else

00:02:50.100 --> 00:02:51.590
entirely…

00:02:51.590 --> 00:02:56.600
Bad days can happen to the best and worst
of us, and sometimes those bad days can spiral

00:02:56.600 --> 00:02:59.620
into very, very bad nights.

00:02:59.620 --> 00:03:02.030
Mike had been having a night like that.

00:03:02.030 --> 00:03:05.450
Earlier that day, he’d lost a fair sum of
money at the races.

00:03:05.450 --> 00:03:11.310
Gambling was one of his many vices, as was
alcohol, and to commiserate his loss, Mike

00:03:11.310 --> 00:03:12.870
had hit the bar.

00:03:12.870 --> 00:03:18.200
Unfortunately, his already foul mood was nudged
into full-blown temper when another patron

00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:20.400
accidentally bumped into him.

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:25.790
The ensuing barfight was a complete disorientated,
drunken mess of glasses being smashed and

00:03:25.790 --> 00:03:27.650
fists thrown.

00:03:27.650 --> 00:03:32.050
One managed to connect hard with Mike’s
jaw, breaking it and leaving him sat on the

00:03:32.050 --> 00:03:33.710
sidewalk in pain.

00:03:33.710 --> 00:03:38.350
Cop cars had shown up, officers breaking up
the ruckus and paramedics arriving to treat

00:03:38.350 --> 00:03:41.010
the more badly injured patrons.

00:03:41.010 --> 00:03:46.150
It was then that two paramedics silently walked
up to Mike and grabbed him by both arms.

00:03:46.150 --> 00:03:50.640
As much as he tried to pull away from their
forceful grip, his arms were covered in bruises

00:03:50.640 --> 00:03:52.520
and cuts from the glass.

00:03:52.520 --> 00:03:57.540
Their fingers dug in, honing in on those painful,
wounded spots so that Mike could really feel

00:03:57.540 --> 00:04:02.090
his own injuries as they pulled him up against
his will.

00:04:02.090 --> 00:04:06.340
Trying to verbally protest only hurt his jaw
further, meaning he could barely call for

00:04:06.340 --> 00:04:12.190
help as he was bundled into the back of an
ambulance, doors slamming shut behind him.

00:04:12.190 --> 00:04:17.230
The next morning introduced Mike to a whole
new and far grizzlier definition of the word

00:04:17.230 --> 00:04:18.630
hangover.

00:04:18.630 --> 00:04:22.680
One of the staff who worked at the bar found
him, just waiting outside when she came to

00:04:22.680 --> 00:04:25.340
open up for business a few days later.

00:04:25.340 --> 00:04:29.340
Sitting out the front, Mike had been left
in the gutter, although it took the barwoman

00:04:29.340 --> 00:04:35.380
a moment to notice just what was wrong with
him… and when she saw it in full, she screamed.

00:04:35.380 --> 00:04:40.210
Instead of Mike’s jaw being fixed, it had
been wrenched open, far wider than natural.

00:04:40.210 --> 00:04:45.680
It was locked in a permanent, gaping expression,
the sides of his lips sporting splits that

00:04:45.680 --> 00:04:49.090
ran all the way into his cheeks.

00:04:49.090 --> 00:04:54.211
Lodged between both rows of Mike’s teeth,
fused to his gums was a piece of glass, too

00:04:54.211 --> 00:04:58.010
thick for him to break to free his jaw or
even bite down on.

00:04:58.010 --> 00:05:03.750
A mouthful of glass shards and blood, cuts
lining the inside of his cheeks, fragments

00:05:03.750 --> 00:05:09.570
lodged in his tongue; all of that might have
been preferable, a mercy compared to what

00:05:09.570 --> 00:05:11.330
had actually happened.

00:05:11.330 --> 00:05:16.050
The glass was keeping his mouth stretched
out, stopping him from speaking like a transparent

00:05:16.050 --> 00:05:17.050
gag.

00:05:17.050 --> 00:05:21.500
And as if not being able to speak or beg for
help wasn’t bad enough, anyone that looked

00:05:21.500 --> 00:05:26.590
through that little window was also offered
a whole other horrific view.

00:05:26.590 --> 00:05:31.430
They could see Mike’s heart, it had been
pulled from his chest and reattached at the

00:05:31.430 --> 00:05:36.120
back of his throat, still beating as tears
rolled down his face.

00:05:36.120 --> 00:05:42.150
He couldn’t eat, talk, only breathing through
his nose… and it hurt.

00:05:42.150 --> 00:05:46.510
Reg and Lee had vowed, when they first got
married, to love each other for better or

00:05:46.510 --> 00:05:51.680
for worse, in sickness and in health, until
death did them part.

00:05:51.680 --> 00:05:54.550
And death very nearly almost parted them.

00:05:54.550 --> 00:05:58.590
If given the choice between dying together,
or suffering through what ended up being done

00:05:58.590 --> 00:06:04.740
to them, not even their love for each other
would have made them want to stay alive.

00:06:04.740 --> 00:06:08.680
The rain was beating down on the windshield
as the couple drove home in silence.

00:06:08.680 --> 00:06:14.420
They’d had a big argument; in fact, it was
small in the grand scheme of their relationship,

00:06:14.420 --> 00:06:15.440
just a lover’s quarrel.

00:06:15.440 --> 00:06:20.419
In that moment, it felt like the biggest problem
in the world, as those types of squabbles

00:06:20.419 --> 00:06:21.419
often do.

00:06:21.419 --> 00:06:26.210
But it would’ve seemed quaint compared to
the fate that awaited both Lee and her husband

00:06:26.210 --> 00:06:27.330
that night.

00:06:27.330 --> 00:06:32.040
Visibility was poor, the headlights were doing
little to help Reg see through the downpour

00:06:32.040 --> 00:06:33.040
or the dark.

00:06:33.040 --> 00:06:37.930
He found it so hard to see, that he almost
missed their turn, quickly wrenching the steering

00:06:37.930 --> 00:06:40.090
wheel to try and correct the mistake.

00:06:40.090 --> 00:06:45.050
Reg lost control of the car as it slid on
the slippery road, flipping sideways and rolling

00:06:45.050 --> 00:06:47.240
as the rain continued to pour.

00:06:47.240 --> 00:06:51.980
The airbags deployed, the force of being thrown
around even with her seatbelt on caused Lee

00:06:51.980 --> 00:06:53.950
to suffer a number of broken ribs.

00:06:53.950 --> 00:06:57.980
Meanwhile, Reg’s arm was broken when the
driver’s side door connected with the ground

00:06:57.980 --> 00:06:59.740
and dented inwards.

00:06:59.740 --> 00:07:03.800
As the couple were left buckled in their seats,
upside down and both crying at the pain of

00:07:03.800 --> 00:07:08.300
their injuries, they spotted the unmistakable
silhouette of an ambulance driving through

00:07:08.300 --> 00:07:10.030
the rain towards them.

00:07:10.030 --> 00:07:13.970
They were both so relieved that neither one
of them realized they hadn’t called the

00:07:13.970 --> 00:07:15.730
emergency number yet.

00:07:15.730 --> 00:07:20.600
Although the rain had long since stopped by
the time Lee woke back up, the storm was just

00:07:20.600 --> 00:07:21.680
beginning.

00:07:21.680 --> 00:07:25.340
Her head was spinning, everything was sore
and aching.

00:07:25.340 --> 00:07:30.650
She had expected to be in a hospital, maybe
with Reg in the bed beside her, both of them

00:07:30.650 --> 00:07:32.979
recovering but alive at least.

00:07:32.979 --> 00:07:38.210
Pushing herself up by her cut, bloody hands,
Lee could feel something heavy behind her,

00:07:38.210 --> 00:07:45.139
a weight on her back like having a rucksack
strapped to her, only it was harder to move,

00:07:45.139 --> 00:07:48.470
almost the same mass as… a person.

00:07:48.470 --> 00:07:53.460
Slowly looking over her shoulder, Lee screamed
when she saw the flesh of her back had been

00:07:53.460 --> 00:08:00.270
fused to Reg’s, their skin melted and stuck
together like candlewax, each of them unable

00:08:00.270 --> 00:08:04.500
to pull away without the pain of feeling like
they were being ripped apart.

00:08:04.500 --> 00:08:07.860
To make matters worse, Lee had undergone…

00:08:07.860 --> 00:08:10.260
Other modifications.

00:08:10.260 --> 00:08:12.690
Talk about in sickness and in health…

00:08:12.690 --> 00:08:16.170
Living alone, Rodney was relatively content
with his life.

00:08:16.170 --> 00:08:20.300
Since retiring, he’d been able to spend
his twilight years appreciating the little

00:08:20.300 --> 00:08:25.530
things, spending most of his time out in the
garden, tending to his flowers and occasionally

00:08:25.530 --> 00:08:28.560
enjoying the company of his adult son.

00:08:28.560 --> 00:08:33.120
Unfortunately, with old age comes the increased
risk of health problems, and to say Rodney

00:08:33.120 --> 00:08:37.779
had himself more than his fair share of heart
difficulties – or a ‘bum ticker’ as

00:08:37.779 --> 00:08:39.899
he called it – was an understatement.

00:08:39.899 --> 00:08:45.130
While out in his garden, Rodney suffered a
violent heart attack and collapsed, wheezing

00:08:45.130 --> 00:08:46.790
and struggling to breathe.

00:08:46.790 --> 00:08:50.879
Luckily, his son, Keith, was in the house
at the time, he witnessed his elderly father

00:08:50.879 --> 00:08:55.290
drop to the ground and ran out to help him,
calling for an ambulance as he tried to calm

00:08:55.290 --> 00:08:56.290
Rodney down.

00:08:56.290 --> 00:09:00.899
The emergency services seemed to arrive much
quicker than Keith had been expecting, a pair

00:09:00.899 --> 00:09:03.990
of paramedics rushing through the house to
lift his dad away.

00:09:03.990 --> 00:09:08.639
What stuck him as strange was, neither one
would tell Keith which hospital they were

00:09:08.639 --> 00:09:12.800
talking his dad to, and they outright refused
to let him ride in the back of the ambulance

00:09:12.800 --> 00:09:17.120
to keep Rodney lucid and reassure him that
he was in safe hands.

00:09:17.120 --> 00:09:20.829
When Keith went to climb into the back, one
of the paramedics pushed him by his chest,

00:09:20.829 --> 00:09:23.310
with enough strength to knock him over.

00:09:23.310 --> 00:09:27.620
As he pulled himself up off the concrete,
the rear doors slammed shut and the ambulance

00:09:27.620 --> 00:09:31.260
sped away to god knows where with Rodney in
the back.

00:09:31.260 --> 00:09:34.800
After a few days of hearing nothing, Keith
had already tirelessly been calling every

00:09:34.800 --> 00:09:38.380
hospital in the area to ask if his dad had
been admitted.

00:09:38.380 --> 00:09:42.860
None of them had seen Rodney, and his worried
son had been just about to call the police

00:09:42.860 --> 00:09:47.589
to file a missing persons report when his
elderly father appeared on the doorstep.

00:09:47.589 --> 00:09:51.899
Immediately, Keith drove his dad to the emergency
room, trying to explain what had happened

00:09:51.899 --> 00:09:53.279
with the strange ambulance.

00:09:53.279 --> 00:09:57.610
While the hospital maintained that it wasn’t
one of theirs, they admitted Rodney and gave

00:09:57.610 --> 00:09:59.600
him a full examination…

00:09:59.600 --> 00:10:05.560
only to find something that would turn the
stomachs of the world’s most seasoned doctors.

00:10:05.560 --> 00:10:08.860
Rodney had more that one heart.

00:10:08.860 --> 00:10:14.420
Someone had given him not just a spare, but
eleven additional hearts.

00:10:14.420 --> 00:10:18.550
They were stuffed between his natural organs
like took many books squeezed together on

00:10:18.550 --> 00:10:19.550
a shelf.

00:10:19.550 --> 00:10:24.430
And not one of them was beating, they were
causing far more harm than good.

00:10:24.430 --> 00:10:28.959
Rodney’s insides were riddled with these
foreign bodies that were stopping his lungs

00:10:28.959 --> 00:10:35.149
from fully inflating, resting on his stomach,
and wreaking havoc with his bodily functions.

00:10:35.149 --> 00:10:39.510
Upon discovery of these extra hearts, Rodney
was rushed into the operating theatre, with

00:10:39.510 --> 00:10:42.459
his son nervously pacing in the corridor outside.

00:10:42.459 --> 00:10:46.879
Sadly, a doctor would soon appear to tell
Keith that the moment the surgeons removed

00:10:46.879 --> 00:10:52.050
one of the additional hearts, Rodney’s old
bum ticker had finally given out.

00:10:52.050 --> 00:10:56.910
Sometimes, as sad as it may be to reconcile
with, tragedy strikes.

00:10:56.910 --> 00:11:01.369
One night, a fire broke out in a crowded bar,
leading to a whole host of people suffering

00:11:01.369 --> 00:11:04.810
severe burns and requiring urgent medical
attention.

00:11:04.810 --> 00:11:08.480
What they received instead was far more brutal
and barbaric.

00:11:08.480 --> 00:11:13.199
Joyce had been in the bar when the alarms
started to ring, nobody knew what had started

00:11:13.199 --> 00:11:14.860
it, only that they needed to evacuate.

00:11:14.860 --> 00:11:19.570
But it didn’t take the flames long to reach
the alcohol behind the bar, and before long

00:11:19.570 --> 00:11:25.790
the whole place was ablaze, everyone panicking
and barging past each other to get out.

00:11:25.790 --> 00:11:29.930
Once free of the searing heat, swapping it
for the biting cold of the night air, the

00:11:29.930 --> 00:11:32.319
commotion didn’t seem to end.

00:11:32.319 --> 00:11:36.379
Someone near her pointed to an ambulance that
had just arrived, and a duo of paramedics

00:11:36.379 --> 00:11:40.459
that were manhandling some of the more badly
burned bar patrons, forcing them into the

00:11:40.459 --> 00:11:41.869
back of their vehicle.

00:11:41.869 --> 00:11:46.059
Along with about six others, Joyce marched
up as the group protested how the injured

00:11:46.059 --> 00:11:47.369
drinkers were being treated.

00:11:47.369 --> 00:11:51.679
When the paramedics refused to stop, things
got uglier.

00:11:51.679 --> 00:11:55.749
The ensuing brawl left Joyce and the other
six people with skull fractures, but rather

00:11:55.749 --> 00:11:59.689
than just leave them behind, the paramedics
grabbed them too.

00:11:59.689 --> 00:12:04.430
Joyce was pushed into an already overcrowded
ambulance, there were twenty-six people crammed

00:12:04.430 --> 00:12:07.300
in there in total, including her.

00:12:07.300 --> 00:12:11.470
Nineteen of them had nasty burns on their
skin, wounds that were only made worse by

00:12:11.470 --> 00:12:16.279
being packed together in such a tight space
and jostled around as the ambulance drove

00:12:16.279 --> 00:12:17.279
away.

00:12:17.279 --> 00:12:20.749
There was no sign of the missing twenty-six
bar patrons for around a week.

00:12:20.749 --> 00:12:24.480
The families of those that had disappeared
after the fire urged the police to keep searching

00:12:24.480 --> 00:12:28.670
for them, with no bodies recovered on the
scene by firefighters.

00:12:28.670 --> 00:12:33.279
Nobody had a clue where the group had gone,
Joyce’s partner, Al, even printed off missing

00:12:33.279 --> 00:12:37.060
flyers and handed them out to anyone who would
take them.

00:12:37.060 --> 00:12:40.999
They also happened to be the caretaker of
a local community centre, and after another

00:12:40.999 --> 00:12:46.240
day of worrying tirelessly about Joyce, Al
moped back there to clean and lock the place

00:12:46.240 --> 00:12:47.240
up.

00:12:47.240 --> 00:12:51.369
What they found waiting for them was like
something out of an old horror B-movie, or

00:12:51.369 --> 00:12:53.779
something found in the deepest parts of the
ocean.

00:12:53.779 --> 00:12:58.050
Filling one of the rooms of the community
center was a huge, watery mass.

00:12:58.050 --> 00:13:03.269
It wasn’t pure liquid, although Al first
mistook it for the result of a leaking pipe.

00:13:03.269 --> 00:13:08.329
The mass was fluid, it twitched and shivered
whenever they reached out to touch it, almost

00:13:08.329 --> 00:13:15.179
like a living thing… or what was left of
a few living things, say twenty-six bar patrons

00:13:15.179 --> 00:13:19.269
melted down and reduced to a collective liquid
mass.

00:13:19.269 --> 00:13:24.019
Now, you’d think having an accident out
in public would be as bad as things got, but

00:13:24.019 --> 00:13:29.329
that’s nothing compared to being injured
in the line of duty, right in the middle of

00:13:29.329 --> 00:13:30.329
a warzone.

00:13:30.329 --> 00:13:31.689
That’s what happened to Private Jackson.

00:13:31.689 --> 00:13:36.869
While he and his squad were out on a routine
patrol in Afghanistan, a group of enemy insurgents

00:13:36.869 --> 00:13:39.480
ambushed the United States’ soldiers.

00:13:39.480 --> 00:13:43.959
During the ensuing firefight, Private Jackson
sustained a severe gunshot wound, leaving

00:13:43.959 --> 00:13:45.360
him bleeding out.

00:13:45.360 --> 00:13:49.989
His comrades had called for a medical evacuation,
and were expecting a US Army helicopter to

00:13:49.989 --> 00:13:51.730
arrive any moment.

00:13:51.730 --> 00:13:57.679
What none of them expected was a city ambulance,
driving towards them across the battlefield

00:13:57.679 --> 00:14:00.990
as if it was the most normal sight on Earth.

00:14:00.990 --> 00:14:04.889
Already suspicious of the approaching vehicle,
Private Jackson’s fellow teammates raised

00:14:04.889 --> 00:14:07.889
their weapons at the approaching paramedics.

00:14:07.889 --> 00:14:12.540
Despite the soldiers demands for them to identify
themselves, neither one of the ambulance attendants

00:14:12.540 --> 00:14:17.529
seemed to pay them much mind, grabbing Private
Jackson and dragging the wounded soldier towards

00:14:17.529 --> 00:14:18.529
the vehicle.

00:14:18.529 --> 00:14:22.499
He called to the rest of his squad, wanted
to be let go, having no idea where he was

00:14:22.499 --> 00:14:24.629
about to be taken or why.

00:14:24.629 --> 00:14:27.649
The commanding officer barked at the pair
of EMTs, warning if they didn’t release

00:14:27.649 --> 00:14:30.769
Private Jackson, then his men would open fire.

00:14:30.769 --> 00:14:33.970
Still, the paramedics didn’t seem to be
listening.

00:14:33.970 --> 00:14:38.089
Just as they threw Jackson into their ambulance
and climbed into the cab at the front, the

00:14:38.089 --> 00:14:40.179
other soldiers opened fire.

00:14:40.179 --> 00:14:43.799
Squeezing their triggers, bullets were spat
from their weapons, riddling the metal sides

00:14:43.799 --> 00:14:48.369
of vehicle as it began to drive away, siren
blaring and lights flashing.

00:14:48.369 --> 00:14:52.759
Every shot that connected with the ambulance
seemed to cause it to leak a viscous black

00:14:52.759 --> 00:14:57.439
fluid, like an oil, but despite this, it did
little to deter the ambulance from driving

00:14:57.439 --> 00:14:59.910
away with Jackson captive in the back.

00:14:59.910 --> 00:15:03.579
After being successfully extracted from the
battlefield, the remainder of the squad were

00:15:03.579 --> 00:15:08.470
airlifted back to safety, arriving back at
their nearby base the following day.

00:15:08.470 --> 00:15:10.589
Each one of them was solemnly silent.

00:15:10.589 --> 00:15:15.509
All of them were confused as to how an ambulance
had appeared in the desert out of nowhere

00:15:15.509 --> 00:15:17.809
and disappeared without a trace.

00:15:17.809 --> 00:15:21.929
But even more so, they were concerned for
the life of their kidnapped comrade.

00:15:21.929 --> 00:15:26.410
However, they wouldn’t have to wait long,
as arriving at their barracks revealed the

00:15:26.410 --> 00:15:29.869
grim, grotesque fate of Private Jackson.

00:15:29.869 --> 00:15:34.839
He was on the walls… as in, all over the
walls.

00:15:34.839 --> 00:15:39.439
His body had been dissolved somehow, broken
down into little more than a thin, bloody

00:15:39.439 --> 00:15:43.930
paste that had now been smeared over the interior
of the barracks.

00:15:43.930 --> 00:15:49.690
Looking out at his former squad from the liquified
remains, was a single human eyeball, Private

00:15:49.690 --> 00:15:54.379
Jackson’s eye, wide with horror at what
had been done to him.

00:15:54.379 --> 00:16:00.170
SCP-4419 – known to some by the nickname
of ‘the Butcher’s Chariot’ – is still

00:16:00.170 --> 00:16:01.170
out there.

00:16:01.170 --> 00:16:06.240
At present, it is unknown who – or indeed
what – performs the horrific mutilations

00:16:06.240 --> 00:16:09.230
on its victims, or even why.

00:16:09.230 --> 00:16:15.319
It could be that SCP-4419, if it has a consciousness,
could be trying to help those it abducts,

00:16:15.319 --> 00:16:18.670
but lacks the correct medical understanding
of how to do so.

00:16:18.670 --> 00:16:23.899
Then again, it could be simply just being
cruel, torturing and deforming people unfortunate

00:16:23.899 --> 00:16:27.040
enough to need emergency medical attention.

00:16:27.040 --> 00:16:31.429
Given how sporadically this anomalous ambulance
can appear and disappear, at the site of any

00:16:31.429 --> 00:16:35.810
medical emergency anywhere on the planet,
there’s little the Foundation can do other

00:16:35.810 --> 00:16:41.949
than stay vigilant and pick up SCP-4419’s
‘patients’ after it has mutilated them…

00:16:41.949 --> 00:16:46.790
or rather, they’ll can pick up whatever’s
left of its victims.

00:16:46.790 --> 00:16:52.279
Now go and check out “SCP-2086 MAN EATING
BUS” for another anomaly that at first takes

00:16:52.279 --> 00:16:57.369
the shape of an ordinary vehicle, but soon
becomes something far more terrifying.

00:16:57.369 --> 00:17:03.179
And after, keep an eye out for “SCP-973
Chased by Smokey” for more horror stalking

00:17:03.179 --> 00:17:03.939
the roads!

